They are derived from openly licensed sources, principally:

  * Wiktionary (English), obtained via the kaikki.org machine-readable extract
    produced by wiktextract — CC BY-SA 4.0 / GFDL.
    https://kaikki.org/dictionary/German/

  * The Tatoeba Project — CC BY 2.0 FR, with some sentences under CC0 1.0.
    Per-sentence ids and authors are retained in sentences/*.json.
    https://tatoeba.org/en/downloads

  * Wikibooks: German — CC BY-SA 4.0.
    https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/German

Share-alike applies: a redistribution of this directory, modified or not, must
carry the same licence and the attributions above.

Each record carries its own `source`, `sourceUrl`/`sourceId` and `license`
fields. See DATA_LICENSES.md in the repository root for the full register and
the modifications made to each source.

EXCEPTION — goethe-levels.json: this file maps 3,277 headwords to A1 / A2 / B1
and is extracted from the Goethe-Institut Wortlisten, which are copyrighted
compilations carrying no redistribution licence. It is NOT covered by the
CC BY-SA 4.0 grant above and is bundled by the repository owner's decision, not
under any licence from the Goethe-Institut. See DATA_LICENSES.md. Delete it and
re-run `npm run data:build` for a directory that is wholly CC BY-SA 4.0.
